IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ma-types`
IMPORT `ma-schedules`
IMPORT `ma-units`
IMPORT `ma-conversion`
IMPORT `ma-orders-saving`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS — Metrication Act 1970. Expected values were decided
-- from the source alone; see independent-expectations.md. A failing
-- assertion is a finding and is left failing.

§ `Independent tests — Metrication Act 1970`

`all units` MEANS LIST metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, candela, hertz, newton, joule, watt, coulomb, volt, farad, ohm, weber, tesla, henry, lumen, lux, radian, steradian, hectare, `metric tonne`, litre, `centigrade or Celsius`, yard, pound, gallon, tahil, kati, chhun, chhek, `another unit`

GIVEN sch IS A Schedule
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep count of` sch MEANS
    count (filter `listed in it` `all units`)
    WHERE
        `listed in it` u MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Schedule row for` u
            WHEN JUST r  THEN r's `schedule` EQUALS sch
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`SI by default` u MEANS `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` FALSE

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`SI, context inconsistent` u MEANS `a unit of the International System of Units:` u `, the context excluding the Fourth Schedule:` TRUE

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`exact row` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule conversion for` u
    WHEN JUST c  THEN c's `exactly`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`approximate row` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule conversion for` u
    WHEN JUST c  THEN NOT c's `exactly`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN u IS A Unit
GIVETH A STRING
`SI unit named for` u MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Third Schedule conversion for` u
    WHEN JUST c  THEN c's `SI unit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "none"

`good order` MEANS `Section 4 order` WITH `replaces references to non-metric units in written law with SI units` IS TRUE, `each replacement is equivalent or a desirable approximation` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette` IS TRUE
`unpublished order` MEANS `Section 4 order` WITH `replaces references to non-metric units in written law with SI units` IS TRUE, `each replacement is equivalent or a desirable approximation` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette` IS FALSE
`bad replacement order` MEANS `Section 4 order` WITH `replaces references to non-metric units in written law with SI units` IS TRUE, `each replacement is equivalent or a desirable approximation` IS FALSE, `published in the Gazette` IS TRUE

§§ `s 3(1) — date`

#ASSERT NOT `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` (YMD 1971 2 14)
#ASSERT `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` (YMD 1971 2 15)
#ASSERT `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` (YMD 2026 10 5)
#ASSERT NOT `the use of SI has legal force and validity in Singapore under s 3(1) on` (YMD 1970 12 31)

§§ `s 2 — SI, SI abbreviation`

#ASSERT `a recognised legal reference to the International System of Units:` "SI"
#ASSERT `SI by default` metre
#ASSERT `SI by default` candela
#ASSERT `SI by default` steradian
#ASSERT `SI by default` radian
#ASSERT `SI by default` hectare
#ASSERT `SI by default` `centigrade or Celsius`
#ASSERT `SI by default` `metric tonne`
#ASSERT `SI by default` litre
#ASSERT NOT `SI, context inconsistent` litre
#ASSERT NOT `SI, context inconsistent` hectare
#ASSERT `SI, context inconsistent` metre
#ASSERT `SI, context inconsistent` joule
#ASSERT NOT `SI by default` yard
#ASSERT NOT `SI by default` chhek
#ASSERT NOT `SI by default` `another unit`

§§ `Schedules 1, 2, 4 — every row`

#ASSERT `indep count of` `the First Schedule` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `indep count of` `the Second Schedule` EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `indep count of` `the Fourth Schedule` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` yard EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` `another unit` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` metre EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "m", "length")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` kilogram EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "kg", "mass")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` second EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "s", "time")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` ampere EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "A", "electric current")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` kelvin EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "K", "thermodynamic temperature")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` candela EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the First Schedule`, "cd", "luminous intensity")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` hertz EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Hz", "frequency")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` newton EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "N", "force")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` joule EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "J", "work, energy, quantity of heat")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` watt EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "W", "power")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` coulomb EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "C", "quantity of electricity, electric charge")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` volt EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "V", "electric tension, potential difference, electromotive force")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` farad EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "F", "electric capacitance")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` ohm EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Ω", "electric resistance")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` weber EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "Wb", "flux of magnetic induction, magnetic flux")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` tesla EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "T", "magnetic flux density, magnetic induction")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` henry EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "H", "inductance")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` lumen EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "lm", "luminous flux")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` lux EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "lx", "illumination")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` radian EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "rad", "plane angle")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` steradian EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Second Schedule`, "sr", "solid angle")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` hectare EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "ha", "area")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` `metric tonne` EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "t", "mass")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` litre EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "L", "volume")
#ASSERT `the Schedule row for` `centigrade or Celsius` EQUALS JUST (`Unit row` OF `the Fourth Schedule`, "°C", "temperature, temperature interval")

§§ `s 5 / Third Schedule — every row`

